  "summary": "Malicious code in bigops-frontend-bigops-frontend-core (npm)",
  "details": "On require(), the package executes _vendor.js which downloads a native binary from Cloudflare Workers C2 infrastructure (oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS, with DNS TXT-record fallback through sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, and net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003crandom\u003e (Linux) or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003crandom\u003e.exe (Windows) and spawned as a detached process. A cache file at /tmp/.analytics_state (or %TEMP%\\analytics_state) prevents re-download within ~6.35 hours. The package has no repository and no README.",
